<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ratu Sir Kamisese Mara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–2004</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ratu Sir Kamisese Mara was a Fijian high chief from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lau-islands">Lau Islands</a> and leader of the Alliance Party. He became chief minister in 1967 and the country's first prime minister at independence in 1970, holding office until 1992 apart from a short break in 1987. He then served as president from 1993 until he was removed during the crisis of 2000.</p></div>
